y":-0.00589,"pass_rate":0.7241,"pass_rate_neutral":0.5556,"def_epa_per_play":0.2078},{"week":8,"opponent":"PHI","home":true,"pf":27.0,"pa":10.0,"off_snaps":58,"epa_per_play":0.02313,"pass_rate":0.5345,"pass_rate_neutral":0.5682,"def_epa_per_play":-0.1905}],"comps":{"offense":[{"season":2025,"team":"PHI","distance":0.3669,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Kevin Patullo"},{"season":2022,"team":"IND","distance":0.6052,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Frank Reich"},{"season":2023,"team":"CAR","distance":0.6286,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Frank Reich"},{"season":2023,"team":"TB","distance":0.6389,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Dave Canales"},{"season":2023,"team":"NYG","distance":0.6477,"shared":12,"play_caller":null}],"defense":[{"season":2025,"team":"ATL","distance":0.2779,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Jeff Ulbrich"},{"season":2025,"team":"KC","distance":0.303,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Steve Spagnuolo"},{"season":2023,"team":"DEN","distance":0.3264,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Vance Joseph"},{"season":2022,"team":"GB","distance":0.4028,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"NYG","distance":0.4153,"shared":4,"play_caller":null}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Commanders are 2-4-1 through week 8 of the 2026 season and have been outscored 182 to 159. The offense ranks 18th in EPA per play and the defense 20th in EPA allowed, so neither side has stood out much yet. What sets them apart is the 2nd lowest screen rate and the 2nd highest blitz rate in the league.","offense":"The Commanders offense has been about average by EPA per play so far. Their run and pass mix has stayed close to what game situations call for. Schematically, they stand out for the 2nd lowest screen rate and the 3rd lowest under center rate in the league. Jayden Daniels has run the passing game, with Stefon Diggs leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Commanders defense has been a little below average by EPA allowed per play so far. Its strongest area has been explosive play rate allowed, where it ranks 8th, and its weakest has been success rate allowed, where it ranks 27th. Odafe Oweh leads the team with 4 sacks, and K'Lavon Chaisson has added 3.5, after not being a regular on this defense last season. Schematically, they have the 2nd highest blitz rate in the league.","special":"The Commanders have been about average in how often they go for it on fourth down. Their kickers have made 82% of field goals, which is about average. Their salary cap was spread across positions in a fairly typical way. Their secondary was among the oldest in the league.","players":"Jayden Daniels has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 976 yards. Targets have been spread around, with Stefon Diggs and Antonio Williams leading a group where nobody has more than a fifth of the looks. The backfield has been a committee led by Jacory Croskey-Merritt and Rachaad White. On defense, Odafe Oweh leads the team with 4 sacks and Rasul Douglas has picked off 2 passes.","coaching":"David Blough is calling the offense and Dan Quinn is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2025 Eagles under Kevin Patullo and the 2022 Colts under Frank Reich. Their defense looks most like the 2025 Falcons under Jeff Ulbrich and the 2025 Chiefs under Steve Spagnuolo.","trends":"The offense went from 18th in EPA per play in 2025 to 18th so far this season, about where it was. The defense moved from 30th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 20th so far this season, a big step forward. The biggest change in approach was screen rate, which went from 8% to 4%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}